{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0140918","isObsolete":false,"name":"centrosomal core","definition":{"text":"The core region of the centrosome, a layered structure containing proteins, surrounded by the centrosomal corona. The core duplicates once per cell cycle at the G2/M transition when two outer layers form the mitotic spindle poles.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"28104305"},{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"30413081"}]},"synonyms":[{"name":"centrosome core","type":"exact"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-03-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2023-11-01","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2023-11-01","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2023-11-01","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2022-10-08","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The core region of the centrosome, a layered structure containing proteins, surrounded by the centrosomal corona. The core duplicates once per cell cycle at the G2/M transition when two outer layers form the mitotic spindle poles."},{"timestamp":"2022-10-08","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0005813 (centrosome)"},{"timestamp":"2022-10-08","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"centrosomal core"},{"timestamp":"2022-10-08","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0110165 (cellular anatomical structure)"},{"timestamp":"2022-10-08","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"centrosome core"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0140918","ancestorName":"centrosomal core","relationship":"never_in_taxon","taxId":"27896","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Planariidae"},{"ancestorId":"GO:0140918","ancestorName":"centrosomal core","relationship":"never_in_taxon","taxId":"33090","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Viridiplantae"},{"ancestorId":"GO:0140918","ancestorName":"centrosomal core","relationship":"never_in_tax